{"ts": "2026-10-27T13:18:31.100412Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1318Z-75fb", "unit": "openspec:add-fake-oidc", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-d4e4e5a6", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied. The authorization handler answers each protocol error of the scenario with a 302 to the registered redirect: response_type other than code gives unsupported_response_type, a scope without openid gives invalid_scope, an absent or malformed code_challenge gives invalid_request, and a code_challenge_method other than S256 gives invalid_request. The redirect carries error, error_description and the unchanged state, and never a code, because the error path builds the Location from the registered redirect_uri with only those parameters. The tracing test passed and asserts, for all four cases, the 302 status, the registered redirect origin and path, the expected error value, state s1 unchanged and the absence of code. Its only deviation from the scenario is that it sends an empty code_challenge rather than omitting the parameter; both values take the same invalid_request branch, and the absent case is handled explicitly in the same condition, so the deviation does ", "text_sha256": "d692319d450dfd70580cd3ab502274268b2de0e61b8ab6af8002ebd7ae2a5a2a", "answer_sha256": "2ef0031404f74041185196206c57a214411fa920af9993968bbe7f79cf7b8826", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-27T13:18:31.113057Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1318Z-75fb", "unit": "openspec:add-fake-oidc", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-005", "target": "F-818a6c14", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding holds. Task 3.1 check 2 says the JWKS must hold at least one key with alg RS256 and non-empty kid, n and e, and the spec says the contract suite must pass on real Keycloak as well as on the fake. checkJwks in contract.ts takes keys[0] and asserts alg RS256 and the fields on that single key, so a JWKS whose first entry is a non-RS256 key (as Keycloak publishes an RSA-OAEP encryption key beside the signing key) fails the check although a valid RS256 key is present. The check must search the array for an RS256 key instead of inspecting the first entry. WHEN the jwks keys check fetches a JWKS whose keys array holds a valid RS256 key with non-empty kid, n and e at any position, with other keys of another alg before it THEN the check resolves, and it still rejects with an AssertionError when no key of the array has alg RS256 with non-empty kid, n and e.", "text_sha256": "f6693b5df187193d70c30d77bd9e22bf966cf8ffca3f44b6f9a7922a8def0d0f", "answer_sha256": "bebeb775eba8514589f6a69594bf40d8c03f6eb114ccf4556a85c06222ee536b", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
